  "summary_en": "Philosophical article on smart-hive biohybrids (e.g., Hiveopolis) combining honeybees, humans and AI-driven robotic technology. Using enactivism and embodied cognition, it argues that ethical concerns about responsibility, care, consent and animal welfare are inseparable from cognition, and that bees merit precautionary moral consideration.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Biohybrid is conceptualised as a triadic bee–human–technology enactive body.",
   "AI is not a moral agent but is never normatively neutral.",
   "Bees should be treated as subjects of ethical concern under a precautionary principle.",
   "Consent and potential harm or benefit to the animals are central ethical questions.",
   "Cites the 2024 New York Declaration on Animal Consciousness as a normative threshold."
